# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file the context is ~1.6 GB (target/ alone), which on a 1 vCPU VPS turns
# `docker compose build` into a multi-minute upload before the first instruction runs.

# Local build artefacts. The image builds its own inside the builder stage; sending the
# host's would also poison the cache with host-linked objects.
/target/

# Secrets. `.env` is never COPYed into any layer, but it must not even enter the build
# context — anything in the context is readable by every build step and by BuildKit's
# cache. Credentials reach the container at runtime via compose `env_file` only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime state — the image ships empty data/logs/reports and compose bind-mounts over
# them. Copying a host database in would silently mix two soaks' statistics.
/data/
/logs/
/reports/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Not needed to compile or run the binary.
/.git/
/.github/
/.claude/
/research/
/docs/
*.md
!README.md
